# Proof: F-V3-INTEGRATION
# Top: tt_um_mcranny_protocol_emulator_v3
#
# Black boxes: v3_engine and v3_pin_cell. Their internal behaviour is proven
# separately by formal/v3_engine.ys and formal/v3_pin_cell.ys, so here they
# are abstracted to their interfaces and their outputs are free. The one
# black-box fact the integration relies on is the pin cell's output-enable
# release contract (pin_oe is low whenever the cell is disabled or in reset),
# which v3_pin_cell.ys proves and which src/v3_project.v re-imposes here as an
# assume on every pin cell's pin_oe inside its generate loop. No other
# black-box assumption is added.
#
# Properties (all in the FORMAL blocks of src/v3_project.v):
#   1. The two ownership masks are disjoint: (own0 & own1) == 0.
#   2. A commit strobe only reaches a pin the strobing engine owns.
#   3. !ena or !rst_n releases every uio_oe bit.
#   4. An accepted START addressing both engines strobes both starts the same
#      cycle, and a rejected START (all-or-nothing) strobes neither engine.
#   5. A program write is refused while the target engine is running.
#   6. The input-filter mask is written only while both engines are stopped.
#
# Method: temporal induction over the integrated wiring with the black-box
# outputs free and the pin-cell release contract assumed. The properties are
# safety properties of the top-level routing and the assumed contract, not of
# any black-boxed block's internal state.
#
# Scope and abstractions: formal/README.md.

# Real sub-blocks (full RTL, no embedded FORMAL assertions).
read_verilog -I src src/v3_timebase.v src/v3_input_filter.v src/v3_host_spi.v \
                     src/v3_progmem.v src/v3_crc.v src/v3_capture.v src/v3_fifo.v

# Blocks to abstract: read only their interfaces (bodies left as black boxes).
read_verilog -lib -I src src/v3_engine.v src/v3_pin_cell.v

# Top with its integration properties and the pin-cell release assume.
read_verilog -formal -DFORMAL -I src src/v3_project.v

hierarchy -top tt_um_mcranny_protocol_emulator_v3
proc

# Abstract the engines and pin cells: deleting their instances leaves their
# output nets undriven, and setundef then drives those nets with fresh free
# ($anyseq) values every cycle. The result is an engine/pin-cell output that
# can take any value, constrained only by the pin-cell release contract that
# src/v3_project.v assumes on each pin_oe.
delete t:v3_engine t:v3_pin_cell
hierarchy -top tt_um_mcranny_protocol_emulator_v3
setundef -undriven -anyseq

flatten
memory_map
opt
async2sync
dffunmap
sat -seq 4 -tempinduct -maxsteps 16 -set-assumes -prove-asserts -verify
